    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9175" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏlŭber</span></b> , bri,
			m.
		akin to celer, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a serpent</i>, <i>snake</i> (<b>poet.</b>), <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2,
				320</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 418</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 2,
				471</span></i> (an imitation of Hom. Il. 22, 93: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δὲ δράκων, κ.τ.λ.</span>); <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
				620</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 775</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 10,
				231</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp., as an attributive of the hair of Medusa, the
			Furies, the Hydra, etc., <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9,
			73</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 6,
			664</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 6, 175</span></i>.</div>
